# TOPSCORE MASTER GOVERNANCE RULES (.antigravityrules)

## DOMAIN 1: CORE ARCHITECTURE, DATA INTEGRITY & POSTGREST SHIELD
1. ABCD ARCHITECTURE:
   - Primary 4-domain structure: [A] Admin, [B] Board, [C] Class, [D] Data.
   - Terminology: Admin, Board, Class, Data, Assessment, Question. NEVER use legacy terms: Affair, Blueprint, or Challenge.
2. FRONTEND SHIELD:
   - ALWAYS use Optional Chaining (`?.`) and fallbacks (`||`, `??`) on DB rows, properties, prerequisites, and metadata. Wrap modals and DOM selectors in defensive existence checks.
3. DATAGRID CELL SANITIZATION:
   - Never render `[object Object]`. Automatically resolve nested dot notation keys to string properties (`.name`, `.title`, `.label`, or formatted JSON fallback).
4. SECURITY & ANSWER KEY PROTECTION:
   - Never leak `correct_answer_snapshot` or `accepted_answers_snapshot` during `IN_PROGRESS` attempts. Return snapshots only for verified finished attempts (`SUBMITTED`, `AUTO_SUBMITTED`, `COMPLETED`, `EXPIRED`).
5. SUPABASE RELATIONSHIP DISAMBIGUATION:
   - Disambiguate multi-foreign-key queries with explicit relationship hints (e.g., `institutions!institution_id(name)`). Maintain defensive in-memory fallback hydration.
6. ERROR HANDLING & RESILIENCE:
   - In `api.js`, gracefully catch Supabase 400/404/network errors. Return empty arrays `[]` or `{}` instead of crashing. Render actionable Error Boundaries with retry options.
7. STRICT UTF-8 ENCODING:
   - Enforce strict UTF-8 across HTML meta tags, API payloads, CSV/Excel parsers, and string sanitizers. Prevent mojibake characters.
8. DATABASE INTEGRITY & SOFT-DELETE:
   - Use Soft-Delete (`deleted_at IS NULL`) exclusively for business entities. NEVER execute raw hard-deletes (`DELETE FROM`) on historical results, attempts, or student records.
9. POSTGREST ASYNC HANDLING:
   - Supabase PostgrestFilterBuilder queries are Thenables, NOT true Promises. Never call `.catch()` directly on them. Always use `try { await ... } catch (err) {}`.
10. DEFENSIVE PROPERTY SCOPING IN UI & MODALS:
    - Explicitly define all counter variables before passing to view layers in modal/quiz loops to prevent `ReferenceError` crashes.

## DOMAIN 2: DESIGN SYSTEM & COLOR SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH
11. SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH COLORING:
    - Never hardcode grade, percentage, points, or answer evaluation colors across CSS or JS modules.
    - All colors must strictly reference `TOPSCORE_COLORS` in `js/grading.js` and corresponding `--grade-*` / `--eval-*` CSS variables in `css/style.css`.
    - Star (★ / 100%) is strictly Electric Pink (`#ff2d87` / RGB `255, 45, 135`) with dark slate text (`#0F172A`) and ambient pink glow. Color is EXCLUSIVE to Star; NEVER inherited by other components.
    - Grade A (90%–99%) is Pure Green (`#00c000ff`) and serves as the sole authoritative green reference for capsules, action buttons, and correct evaluations (`--eval-correct`).
    - Grade B: Electric Lime (`#95ff00ff`), Grade C: Pure Yellow (`#FFFF00`), Grade D: Dark Orange (`#FF8C00`), Grade E: Pure Red (`#FF0000`).
    - Round grade badges (`.grade-circle`): ALL symbols and letters (★, A, B, C, D, E) strictly render dark slate (`#0F172A`), universally eliminating white text.
    - Points (PTS) dynamically follow `getGradeColorByScore()`.

## DOMAIN 3: SPATIAL LAYOUT, TABLE ARCHITECTURE & UI INVARIANTS
15. UNIVERSAL TABLE ARCHITECTURE & ZERO PAGE SCROLL (STRICT INVARIANT) (/learn):
    - Root `html` & `body`: `height: 100vh !important; max-height: 100vh !important; width: 100vw !important; overflow: hidden !important; margin: 0 !important; padding: 0 !important;`.
    - Locked base footer (`#bottom-ad-banner` / `.topscore-locked-banner`): fixed 60px height. Layout `#admin-console`: `height: calc(100vh - 60px) !important; max-height: calc(100vh - 60px) !important;` (zero outer scroll).
    - Table-Only Vertical Scroll: Vertical scrolling is permitted EXCLUSIVELY inside table body containers (`.table-wrap` / `tbody`). Sticky headers (`thead th` top: 0), sticky footers (`tfoot` bottom: 0; empty collapse: `tfoot:empty { display: none !important; }`).
    - Action toolbars: `flex: 0 0 auto !important; height: auto !important; min-height: 0 !important;`. When Edit Mode is OFF, toolbars containing only hidden `.edit-mode-only` buttons must completely collapse (`display: none !important; margin: 0 !important; padding: 0 !important;`). Designate grid containers with `flex: 1 1 0 !important; min-height: 0 !important;`.
16. PURE DIRECT ENGLISH UI STANDARD (/learn):
    - All UI, navigation menus, tab titles, table headers, status labels, buttons, tooltips, dialogs, toasts, and system messages across all pages (`index.html`, `dashboard.html`, `test.html`, `result.html`, `admin.html`) must use direct, professional English.
    - Sole exception: Indonesian vocabulary meaning inside Vocabulary Vault (`vocabulary_vault.meaning`).
17. SINGLE-RESPONSIBILITY COLUMNS (1 INFO = 1 COLUMN) (/learn):
    - Every table column across all pages must strictly contain ONLY ONE metric or item. Never concatenate multiple distinct metrics into a single cell.
18. NO-CAPSULE VIEW MODE & EDIT-MODE-ONLY CAPSULES (/learn):
    - View mode (Edit Mode OFF): zero capsules, bordered pill boxes, or badges around data cells, scores, or statuses. Render clean, flat text with `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`.
    - Capsule styling is strictly reserved for interactive editable inputs/steppers, appearing ONLY when Master Edit Mode is ON (`body.global-edit-mode-on`).
20. UNIVERSAL LOWER PANEL ARCHITECTURE & 10PX CONTAINER GAP (/learn):
    - Lower panel & table footers (`tfoot`): strictly `height: 50px !important; min-height: 50px !important; max-height: 50px !important; box-sizing: border-box;`, matching the 50px sidebar footer (`.sidebar-footer`).
    - All containers, panels, cards, and tables must maintain an exact 10px gap (`gap: 10px !important;` or `margin-bottom: 10px !important;`).
21. DYNAMIC COLUMN SIZING, SINGLE-LINE TEXT & ZERO DEAD SPACE INVARIANT (/learn):
    - Zero dead space: tables expand to 100% width (`width: 100% !important;`). Dynamic content sizing (`table-layout: auto;`).
    - Table cell text must NEVER wrap onto multiple lines (`white-space: nowrap !important; text-overflow: ellipsis; overflow: hidden;`). Uniform balanced typography (`0.78rem`–`0.8rem`). No clipped text.
22. CENTERED LOADING STATES & CANONICAL COMPONENT INVARIANT (/learn):
    - All loading indicators and spinners in Tutor's Room must strictly render centered horizontally and vertically (`display: flex !important; flex-direction: column !important; align-items: center !important; justify-content: center !important; width: 100% !important; height: 100% !important; min-height: calc(100vh - 200px) !important; flex: 1 1 0 !important; margin: auto !important; box-sizing: border-box !important;`).
    - Parent containers (`#class-hub-tab-content`, `.workspace-content`) must enforce `width: 100% !important; height: 100% !important; flex: 1 1 0 !important;` to eliminate horizontal side-drifting. Canonical helper: `getLoadingStateHtml(message)`. Direct English only.
25. TUTOR'S ROOM 8-TIER TYPOGRAPHIC SCALE & ZERO SUB-11PX INVARIANT (/learn):
    - 8-tier scale tokens: Display (20px Outfit 800), Title (16px Outfit 700), Subtitle (14px Inter 600), Body (13px Inter 500), Table (12px Inter 500/700), Control (12px Inter 600), Caption (11px Inter 600), Mono (11px Mono 600).
    - Zero Sub-11px Rule: No text element in Tutor's Room may render smaller than 11px. Eradicate legacy `0.65rem` (8.3px), `0.70rem` (8.9px), `8pt`, and `8.5pt`.
    - Standard data cells use weight 500; bold 700/800 is reserved for headers/titles. Purge unneeded italics on dark surfaces.

